# Cypress Nightly Report Audit

A Claude Code skill that reads the Jenkins Cypress nightly report and finds the real problems behind the red tests. It shows them on a dashboard and fixes them one at a time, only after you say yes.

Command: `/cypress-nightlyreportaudit`

---

## What it does

Every night, Jenkins runs the Cypress suite and produces a report. Often more than 100 tests fail, but most of them share a few causes. This skill:

1. Finds the newest report on your computer.
2. Reads every failed test, with the full error message.
3. Saves the result in a history, so it can compare nights.
4. Sorts each failure into a group (see [Failure groups](#failure-groups)).
5. Builds a dashboard with the pass-rate trend and a ranked list of fixes.
6. Fixes the test code one candidate at a time, after you confirm each edit.

It never edits test code on its own.

