## The healer agents

The skill works with two agents in `.claude/agents/`.

| | `cypress-report-healer` | `cypress-self-healer` |
|---|---|---|
| Starts from | The nightly report | One spec you name |
| Decides what to fix | Yes. It ranks the failures and suggests an order. | No, you choose |
| How it fixes | Uses the self-healer's method, one spec at a time | Runs the spec in Chrome, scans the live page with `tools/dom-digest.js`, and fixes the selector or the wait |
| Use it when | You want to fix last night's failures | You already know which spec is broken |

The report-healer chooses what to fix and in which order. The self-healer does the fixing.

How the report-healer heals a spec:
1. It runs the spec locally once, before any change.
2. It compares the local result with the report.
3. It fixes it in at most 3 runs: one to find the problem, one to check the fix, one clean run to confirm.
4. It writes the result to `.claude/cypress-audit/heal-reports/<date>.md`.

